{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae","id":21487,"title":"Hunter: Mortal Remains Preview - The Faithful of Shulpae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T01:08:39-08:00","id":21487,"title":"Hunter: Mortal Remains Preview - The Faithful of Shulpae","content":"I posted something over at the Onyx Path blog page you might be interested in seeing. It's a Conspiracy from Mortal Remains. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunter the Vigil: The Faithful of Shulpae &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-the-vigil-the-faithful-of-shulpae/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:12:02-08:00","id":21495,"title":"","content":"This looks really good, is this open development style? Because I have a few comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A group of hunters with Anthropophagy can share a single corpse, but <u>must split the desired Dread Power dots between each other</u>, the character with the highest Anthropophagy dots gets first pick. </div> </div> </div> The underlined section here implies there's some kind of &quot;dread power economy&quot; when the rest of the paragraph makes it clear that it's a &quot;pound of flesh economy&quot;. Changing it to&quot;<br /> <br /> A group of hunters with Anthropophagy can share a single corpse, but the monster must have enough flesh to feed the entire group...<br /> <br /> would probably be clearer.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The human stomach is not meant to process that much raw flesh. For every pound devoured in excess of her Stamina dots, she suffers one lethal damage from the engorgement. </div> </div> </div> I'd use the toxins subsystem here rather than engorgement. Assuming an average of Stamina 2, the typical person would be spending three days recuperating from eating what amounts to the meat form 12 McDonalds quarter ponders. Now I admit that's a lot of food, but IMO it's not enough to spend three days with a serious injury. Toxins just make more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s worth noting that murdering and eating a person is an Integrity breaking point. Make the breaking point roll at a penalty equal to the hunter\u2019s Anthropophagy dots. </div> </div> </div> I'm assuming that this dosn't stop becoming a breaking point after the first time because of the murder is always a breaking point rule; but how would this work with The Code?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:18:06-08:00","id":21498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21495#post21495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks really good, is this open development style? Because I have a few comments.<br /> <br /> The underlined section here implies there's some kind of &quot;dread power economy&quot; when the rest of the paragraph makes it clear that it's a &quot;pound of flesh economy&quot;. Changing it to&quot;<br /> <br /> A group of hunters with Anthropophagy can share a single corpse, but the monster must have enough flesh to feed the entire group...<br /> <br /> would probably be clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only so much flesh. But the monster has to have the Dread Powers to support the feast. So if you have a monster with Blast 1, you can't have five dudes eat it and all get Blast 1. I'll fuss with the wording a little bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21495#post21495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd use the toxins subsystem here rather than engorgement. Assuming an average of Stamina 2, the typical person would be spending three days recuperating from eating what amounts to the meat form 12 McDonalds quarter ponders. Now I admit that's a lot of food, but IMO it's not enough to spend three days with a serious injury. Toxins just make more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently you've never eaten three Big Macs. Let alone three pounds of raw beef. We toyed around with it. The people playing said it was easier to just use immediate damage for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21495#post21495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming that this dosn't stop becoming a breaking point after the first time because of the murder is always a breaking point rule; but how would this work with The Code?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using The Code, you'll have to reconcile that at your table. Eating people's pretty hardcore stuff. I'd probably not allow it to apply. But if you wanted, that's up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:26:07-08:00","id":21501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21498#post21498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only so much flesh. But the monster has to have the Dread Powers to support the feast. I'll fuss with the wording a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok that bit makes more sense now I know what it was supposed to mean, best of luck fussing with the wording <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21498#post21498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently you've never eaten three Big Macs. Let alone three pounds of raw beef. We toyed around with it. The people playing said it was easier to just use immediate damage for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> How did you guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was always a chicken nugget person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21498#post21498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using The Code, you'll have to reconcile that at your table. Eating people's pretty hardcore stuff. I'd probably not allow it to apply. But if you wanted, that's up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always understood it that The Code was supposed to be about the hardcore stuff. I mean, a long term Vigil is Morality 2 under the old system (hunting monsters is quite often planned murder, doing it several times bumps it up to serial murder).<br /> <br /> While The Codes core purpose was to let you play a hunter without your morality plummeting to nothingness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-02-2013, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:27:33-08:00","id":21502,"title":"","content":"This is excellent material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:32:18-08:00","id":21504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21501#post21501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always understood it that The Code was supposed to be about the hardcore stuff. I mean, a long term Vigil is Morality 2 under the old system (hunting monsters is quite often planned murder, doing it several times bumps it up to serial murder).<br /> <br /> While The Codes core purpose was to let you play a hunter without your morality plummeting to nothingness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is and it isn't. In my experience, Hunter's all about the gray areas. Debating and discussing what constitutes a violation, and what doesn't. That said, Integrity's a slightly different beast than Morality, so it interacts a little differently, and having a low rating doesn't actually mean the same thing. <br /> <br /> More to the point, there's killing, then there's eating things to gain their superpowers. I might allow the former under certain circumstances, or with The Code. But the latter? It's ickypants, no matter who you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:42:59-08:00","id":21506,"title":"","content":"I agree that hunter is very much about the grey areas, but I always interpreted that as &quot;what should your Code say?&quot;, rather than &quot;what can your Code say?&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to say that &quot;monsters don't count&quot; (isn't that the example used in the books? My copy is at home) and define a monster as anything with supernatural powers; you <i>could</i> do that. It's permitted under the mechanical rules for The Code. But <i>should</i> you do that? Probably not, because a lot of supernatural things don't deserve to be killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's the same here. Maybe I just have odd views but I would say that killing people is worse than eating corpses; I mean, I genuinely think that killing an innocent changeling because of prejudice, or even killing a guilty changeling instead of giving it a fair trial and sentencing it via Pledge, is far worse than eating a Mummy.<br /> <br /> Mummies come back, a Changeling's death is final.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:58:18-08:00","id":21513,"title":"","content":"Because every hunter knows and cares that a changeling dies but a mummy comes back.<br /> <br /> Except, you know, everyone who doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T02:59:10-08:00","id":21514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21506#post21506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that hunter is very much about the grey areas, but I always interpreted that as &quot;what should your Code say?&quot;, rather than &quot;what can your Code say?&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to say that &quot;monsters don't count&quot; (isn't that the example used in the books? My copy is at home) and define a monster as anything with supernatural powers; you <i>could</i> do that. It's permitted under the mechanical rules for The Code. But <i>should</i> you do that? Probably not, because a lot of supernatural things don't deserve to be killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's the same here. Maybe I just have odd views but I would say that killing people is worse than eating corpses; I mean, I genuinely think that killing an innocent changeling because of prejudice, or even killing a guilty changeling instead of giving it a fair trial and sentencing it via Pledge, is far worse than eating a Mummy.<br /> <br /> Mummies come back, a Changeling's death is final.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, this is killing THEN eating the corpse. You're not just eating a corpse, you're killing with the intent to eat. Killing something because it's a monster terrorizing your neighborhood, that's a gray area. Killing something because you will learn to turn into a dust storm if you eat it? That's not very gray to me. <br /> <br /> But yeah, that's pretty much the stance. Killing should count, unless you're going hardcore splatterpunk or some shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:08:16-08:00","id":21517,"title":"","content":"so the Amkhat returned from the dead, I see? And all of their beliefs reminds me of an idea for a conspiracy I once had.. well, one less idea to work on!<br /> <br /> And yeah, while the Code in theory could, killing someone and eating him without consequences is not really my cup of tea :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:27:32-08:00","id":21529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21513#post21513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because every hunter knows and cares that a changeling dies but a mummy comes back.<br /> <br /> Except, you know, everyone who doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well every hunter hopes that the monsters they kill aren't coming back (it's a pretty safe assumption all things considered), and I got the impression the faithful know mummies come back. They quite like the ability to eat and then re-eat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21514#post21514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind, this is killing THEN eating the corpse. You're not just eating a corpse, you're killing with the intent to eat. Killing something because it's a monster terrorizing your neighborhood, that's a gray area. Killing something because you will learn to turn into a dust storm if you eat it? That's not very gray to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah. It is an objectively immoral motivation.<br /> <br /> The actions aren't as bad, but the motivation is far more immoral; but now were edging onto stuff like consequentialist vs deontological ethics, and the philosophers still haven't decided on that one and they probably never will.<br /> <br /> <br /> But basically speaking. My point is that I don't see The Code as having a lower limit. Once you start justifying campaigns of pre-meditated serial murder because &quot;monster's don't count&quot;. You're pretty much as low as you can go already.<br /> <br /> It just seems weird that the rules might say serial murder out of pure naked prejudice is mechanically supported by The Code, but doing it for power is too far for the The Code to work.<br /> <br /> And you know, I kinda like the fact that The Code supports such objectively horrible actions with no lower limit. As Slasher shows, the risk of going too far is a great theme to mine. To me the moment your Code says &quot;eating monsters to get their sweet sweet magic is totally ok!&quot; you're already taken a big step down the slippery slope. (You could argue that The Faithful slid to the bottom long ago) but the idea of measuring steps downwards by how bad your Code is really appeals to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21517#post21517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, while the Code in theory could, killing someone and eating him without consequences is not really my cup of tea :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the sort of Code I'd give to antagonistic Hunter NPCs but not protagonists. (I mean, if I was storytelling I'd let players take it, but only after saying OOC that if they go through with it they've taken a step towards becoming a Slasher or something along that line)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-02-2013, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:32:30-08:00","id":21530,"title":"","content":"Knows AND Cares. Also, apply equally to both mummy and changeling.<br /> <br /> Or put another way, stop looking from the top down as a person reading a book and ask yourself how you'd feel under the limited knowledge you'd have as a hunter. Killing a changeling doesn't look half as bad as eating a mummy,dead or alive, on the street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:43:01-08:00","id":21536,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Killing does look worse than eating. (Killing AND eating is worse than killing alone; but IMO it's weird to draw the line between &quot;killing&quot; and &quot;killing and eating&quot;. If there is a line it should be long before killing but to me; I like the fact there's no line at all for The Code. I think it works great for modeling things like the descent into a Slasher)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-02-2013, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T03:52:30-08:00","id":21539,"title":"","content":"Why should there only be one line? It's not like doing one thing opens a whole new world of options to you-more likely it just opens the ones nearest you first, and even that's with some trepidation.<br /> <br /> There are no cliffs in what we become numb to, just long gentle slopes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T04:10:59-08:00","id":21545,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by that. Isn't that agreeing with what I said? That there shouldn't be a hard line beyond which the mechanical subsystems of The Code no longer apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T04:13:56-08:00","id":21548,"title":"","content":"What I was disagreeing with you on was the idea that killing a changeling is worse than eating a mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T04:25:18-08:00","id":21552,"title":"","content":"Ok. We disagree but I think we may as well leave it at that. Debating morality is hard and It's kinda off topic since my primary point was that there shouldn't be a lower limit beyond which The Code should not reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T04:55:01-08:00","id":21557,"title":"","content":"Awesome, horrible stuff. Looking forward to the release","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:20:02-08:00","id":21604,"title":"","content":"This is fine material and I hope this reflect the quality of the overall book. I can also see how such a Conspiracy could exist in the WOD, and introducing it in game would be great to add to the &quot;dark side&quot; of Hunter. But I don't see any person in my gaming band who would have the stomach (pun intented) to play a member of such a group, it goes to much against the mood of our games. If the Faithful of Shulpae are introduce in one of our session, it will likely be as foes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/8.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","name":"Kergonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T07:24:21-08:00","id":21606,"title":"","content":"I'm ok with the occasional hunter group that's antagonist only. The Promethean Brotherhood is another example out there and arguably Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> BTW, I was wondering. Would Unbound Geists/Sin-Eaters have the Revivification Dread-Power? There's quite a bit about eating in Geist and that makes these guys great Sin-Eater Antagonists too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:30:07-08:00","id":21645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21606#post21606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm ok with the occasional hunter group that's antagonist only. The Promethean Brotherhood is another example out there and arguably Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> BTW, I was wondering. Would Unbound Geists/Sin-Eaters have the Revivification Dread-Power? There's quite a bit about eating in Geist and that makes these guys great Sin-Eater Antagonists too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't THINK Sin-Eaters inherently have it, but I might be wrong. That draft's been out of my hands for a while. But it's certainly one that could make a lot of sense for them. <br /> <br /> And FYI, it looks like this: <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Revivify (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> A creature with this Dread Power is nigh unstoppable. They\u2019ll die like anything else, but that\u2019s not the end of their rampage. They can return from the grave quickly, albeit weakened. This Dread Power takes a hefty toll on the monster, however, causing irreparable harm to the body. This is, of course, a small price to pay for immortality. <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1Willpower and 1 dot of Stamina <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina + Survival + Revivify<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Dread Power can only be activated when the monster is effectively dead \u2014 that is incapacitated \u2014 with a health track full of lethal damage. It must be used within one day of death for each dot of the Dread Power. The monster spends Willpower and a permanent dot of Stamina (or Resistance, if using disembodied traits). If successful, the monster rises from death, slightly less injured. Each success on the dice roll removes two bashing damage, or one lethal damage. <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The monster not only stays dead, but cannot attempt to use Revivify ever again. Death is permanent. <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The monster does not rise, but loses the Willpower and dot of Stamina. If he still has Stamina and Willpower remaining, he can attempt again. <br /> <b>Success:</b> The monster rises, unless his entire health track is full of aggravated damage. Successes heal two bashing or one lethal damage each. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The monster rises, and rises fully healed of all damage, aggravated or otherwise. <br /> <b>Note:</b> The monster cannot use this power if it only has a single dot of Stamina. At that point, the monster is permanently destroyed. If completely full of aggravated damage, the monster can only resurrect with an exceptional success on the activation roll. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:34:54-08:00","id":21647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21645#post21645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't THINK Sin-Eaters inherently have it, but I might be wrong. That draft's been out of my hands for a while. But it's certainly one that could make a lot of sense for them.<br /> <br /> And FYI, it looks like this:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Revivify (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> A creature with this Dread Power is nigh unstoppable. They\u2019ll die like anything else, but that\u2019s not the end of their rampage. They can return from the grave quickly, albeit weakened. This Dread Power takes a hefty toll on the monster, however, causing irreparable harm to the body. This is, of course, a small price to pay for immortality.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1Willpower and 1 dot of Stamina<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Stamina + Survival + Revivify<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Dread Power can only be activated when the monster is effectively dead \u2014 that is incapacitated \u2014 with a health track full of lethal damage. It must be used within one day of death for each dot of the Dread Power. The monster spends Willpower and a permanent dot of Stamina (or Resistance, if using disembodied traits). If successful, the monster rises from death, slightly less injured. Each success on the dice roll removes two bashing damage, or one lethal damage.<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The monster not only stays dead, but cannot attempt to use Revivify ever again. Death is permanent.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The monster does not rise, but loses the Willpower and dot of Stamina. If he still has Stamina and Willpower remaining, he can attempt again.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The monster rises, unless his entire health track is full of aggravated damage. Successes heal two bashing or one lethal damage each.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The monster rises, and rises fully healed of all damage, aggravated or otherwise.<br /> <b>Note:</b> The monster cannot use this power if it only has a single dot of Stamina. At that point, the monster is permanently destroyed. If completely full of aggravated damage, the monster can only resurrect with an exceptional success on the activation roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why is the power dots listed 1 to 5 if there is no mechanics for the levels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:40:25-08:00","id":21651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21647#post21647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why is the power dots listed 1 to 5 if there is no mechanics for the levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its dots add to your dice pool. Your dice pool gives you your only chance at surviving death by aggravated damage, and the dice pool will ultimately determine how much health you revivify with. It also determines how many days dead you can be before revivifying. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:56:09-08:00","id":21667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21651#post21651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its dots add to your dice pool. Your dice pool gives you your only chance at surviving death by aggravated damage, and the dice pool will ultimately determine how much health you revivify with. It also determines how many days dead you can be before revivifying.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, I forgot to pay attention to the die roll &gt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T08:58:16-08:00","id":21672,"title":"","content":"The cool thing is that this aggravated rule means that there's actually a practical advantage to feeding monsters into a wood-chipper to max out the Aggravated. I might go a bit further and say that really through stuff like burning the body or a wood chipper gives a negative modifier to the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:03:16-08:00","id":21674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21506#post21506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same here. Maybe I just have odd views but I would say that killing people is worse than eating corpses; I mean, I genuinely think that killing an innocent changeling because of prejudice, or even killing a guilty changeling instead of giving it a fair trial and sentencing it via Pledge, is far worse than eating a Mummy.<br /> <br /> Mummies come back, a Changeling's death is final.</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys would have this conversation as I am currently eating lunch and now I can't help but think of the bagel across from me would act as a changeling.<br /> <br /> I think the NPC would be delicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:50:39-08:00","id":21720,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the discussion's moral implications is Morality vs Integrity. Integrity doesn't represent how moral you are, its roll is always the same, and may get bonuses quite differently from morality. It is more of a measure of sanity, grip, and hold to normalcy than morality, rather than having those as consequential issues associated with low morality.<br /> <br /> How the code applies to Integrity, without a set list of sins is a very different matter Kings Raven. You seemed to ignore that this system has moved to Integrity rather than staying at morality, and that may be a major fault in your argument. Your arguing from different standpoints.<br /> <br /> Integrity has no set sin structure, only penalties associated with the severity of sins (-5 for premeditated murder being the biggest penalty). The witnessing of various supernatural events are generally breaking points which makes it very different from how Morality was before.<br /> <br /> The Code might work entirely different under GMC rules, giving bonuses or eliminating penalties instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:02:43-08:00","id":21734,"title":"","content":"Unless there is a modified alternative hunter-integrity or hunter-code (which I think I can be forgiven for not knowing about; and assume machineIV would have mentioned) I think that my point still holds.<br /> <br /> The Doylist purpose of The Code is to adapt Morality for a different game with different assumptions. So I assume that post-GMC The Code will serve the same purpose: to adapt Integrity to a game with completely different assumptions. Notice that the GMC has a rule saying that murder is always a Breaking Point with a massive penalty. A straight forward &quot;kill monsters&quot; hunter game would quickly turn everyone to Integrity 0, hence why there's need for The Code. It both defeats the purpose of the morality/integrity system if it's fall to nothing is quick and inevitable, and it goes against the theme of hunters being incredibly tough individuals with the grit to take on vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:45:35-08:00","id":21763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21734#post21734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless there is a modified alternative hunter-integrity or hunter-code (which I think I can be forgiven for not knowing about; and assume machineIV would have mentioned) I think that my point still holds.<br /> <br /> The Doylist purpose of The Code is to adapt Morality for a different game with different assumptions. So I assume that post-GMC The Code will serve the same purpose: to adapt Integrity to a game with completely different assumptions. Notice that the GMC has a rule saying that murder is always a Breaking Point with a massive penalty. A straight forward &quot;kill monsters&quot; hunter game would quickly turn everyone to Integrity 0, hence why there's need for The Code. It both defeats the purpose of the morality/integrity system if it's fall to nothing is quick and inevitable, and it goes against the theme of hunters being incredibly tough individuals with the grit to take on vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that morality has an entirely different mechanic from Integrity. There aren't set dice pools, there are a number of different associated bonuses and penalties instead. There are no &quot;in stone&quot; hierarchy of sins. Hunters with high resolve+composure scores are nearly immune to losing integrity. There are a number of bonuses that can be applied, such as acting with your virtue and other such ways of modifying the roll.<br /> <br /> Integrity is very different from the Morality mechanics and to just assume that a system developed to make hunter more like integrity in the first place works the same is flawed. The mechanical effects of the code, eliminating certain things through justification is essentially built into Integrity. There are a few &quot;Hard Sins&quot; like murder, but associating that murdering monsters is one thing. Eating something to gain magical power is an entirely different concept from say murder in a morality system. It isn't as much a matter of being moral, its a matter of involving yourself heavily in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Equate it to the sanity mechanics in mirrors. As sanity drops you can gain supernatural powers. This is essentially the wear on integrity that eating something for power is. It isn't a moral standpoint, its a normalcy standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:38:48-08:00","id":21795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21763#post21763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Equate it to the sanity mechanics in mirrors. As sanity drops you can gain supernatural powers. This is essentially the wear on integrity that eating something for power is. It isn't a moral standpoint, its a normalcy standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's where you're going wrong. Integrity isn't a normalcy metric. It measures psychological stress, and the damage thereof. Therefore involving yourself in the supernatural dosn't have to decrease Integrity. It <i>can</i>, the supernatural is scary, dangerous and stressful, but it doesn't have too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now you can certainly argue that The Code needs updating to a shiny new GMC set of rules to work with Integrity (who knows, perhaps it's in Mortal Remains); but I think my core points hold: <br /> 1) Hunter does need mechanical tweaks to the Integrity system, or Merits that affect it. Things like murder always being a Breaking Point roll are mechanically inappropriate for a game where serial killers (of monsters) are the assumed protagonists.<br /> 2) There's no reason why the Hunter ability to immunise themselves to Breaking Points shouldn't extend to icky magic rituals, as well as murder. I believe that immunising yourself to icky stuff is a great way to tell a story of the slide down the slippery slope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:59:28-08:00","id":21807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> GMC<br /> Integrity measures how well a character<br /> can cope with the traumatic and supernatural events of his<br /> life.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The character performs an action that either violates his personal moral code or that is considered unacceptable in society.<br /> \u2022 The character witnesses something traumatic, terrifying, or that rattles his understanding of the world.<br /> \u2022 The character is the victim of a supernatural attack,<br /> whether physical, emotional, or mental. </div> </div> </div>Those are the categories of breaking points for integrity. I would figure that a hunter at first would have issues that are rattling his understanding of the world, but would later be. Eating someone for magical power is certainly rattling world understanding as you gain supernatural powers from it. Then there's the long list of modifiers associated as well. David seems to indicate that hunters are using Integrity. While the Code(Or Banes) is relatively appropriate in a structural hierarchy like Humanity, in a system that is only loosely structured and pretty well has &quot;The Code&quot; built in, it isn't quite the same.<br /> <br /> You could simply argue that killing a Monster doesn't count after the first few times or so, because its a monster. That would be perfectly legitimate. However, performing ritualized eating of monsters to gain entirely new insight into the world in a supernatural way is radically different and unlikely to be something &quot;Normal.&quot; Each time they eat one they learn something radically different, absorbing a piece of this 'thing' into themselves. I'd say its so different each time that its something that you simply don't get use to, it isn't about justifying it like the code, its about armoring yourself against such an experience.<br /> <br /> Hunter's lives are ambiguous on morality yes, but there are things like vampires that work at soup kitchens and strive to make up for their monstrous nature. Does this count the same as the vampire dealing drugs to and then killing school children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T12:20:48-08:00","id":21824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21807#post21807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could simply argue that killing a Monster doesn't count after the first few times or so, because its a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div> Humans too. This is not a good thing.<br /> <br /> I would say that Slashers don't risk Integrity for murdering a human. That's what makes them a Slasher, killing is just <i>normal</i> to them. (Incidently, if I was STing and a player said to me they wanted to add a Code saying that Ashwood Abbey doesn't count, I'd say yes; then give them the Avenger Undertaking).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21807#post21807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be perfectly legitimate. However, performing ritualized eating of monsters to gain entirely new insight into the world in a supernatural way is radically different and unlikely to be something &quot;Normal.&quot; Each time they eat one they learn something radically different, absorbing a piece of this 'thing' into themselves. I'd say its so different each time that its something that you simply don't get use to, it isn't about justifying it like the code, its about armoring yourself against such an experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> Touch\u00e9. This is a much better argument than MachineIV's.<br /> <br /> MachineIV said that the reason Feasting is a breaking point is because cannibalism is ickypants. If you can become immunised to murdering monsters then IMO you can become immunised to ickypants. On the other hand no matter how tough you are, using a magical ritual to alter your mind is dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21807#post21807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter's lives are ambiguous on morality yes, but there are things like vampires that work at soup kitchens and strive to make up for their monstrous nature. Does this count the same as the vampire dealing drugs to and then killing school children?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that it depends on the individual hunter; but a hunter could say Vampire is a Vampire is a Vampire; and then kill both those example vampires without having to roll for a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Codes that are just too broad are a bad thing, and a step down the slippery slope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T12:29:36-08:00","id":21830,"title":"","content":"Woohoo, a Conspiracy from the new book that adds to my own in-game list without making me drop anything!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:15:04-08:00","id":21851,"title":"","content":"I'm lovin' it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:40:50-08:00","id":21933,"title":"","content":"&quot;They're eating her! And then they're gonna eat me!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:57:57-08:00","id":21949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21933#post21933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;They're eating her! And then they're gonna eat me!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh my JUUUUUUUDGE!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:59:41-08:00","id":21952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21851#post21851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm lovin' it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The McDonald's version of this Conspiracy is so much scarier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T21:39:52-08:00","id":22110,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see in the comments it's confirmed that there is (in addition to the Faithful) Arisen targeted Compact, a Demon targeted Compact, and a Demon targeted Conspiracy. That means the only conflict I may have (with my ocd need for an organized list of player options for my table) is with the Demon Conspiracy. I'm currently working on the Xuanmiao Ministry as China's para-governmental Hunter Conspiracy who use harnessed God Machine based tech to capture and program supernaturals into their agents. I am excited to see what alternative OP offers me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T01:13:17-08:00","id":22195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22110#post22110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see in the comments it's confirmed that there is (in addition to the Faithful) Arisen targeted Compact, a Demon targeted Compact, and a Demon targeted Conspiracy. That means the only conflict I may have (with my ocd need for an organized list of player options for my table) is with the Demon Conspiracy. I'm currently working on the Xuanmiao Ministry as China's para-governmental Hunter Conspiracy who use harnessed God Machine based tech to capture and program supernaturals into their agents. I am excited to see what alternative OP offers me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Demon-centric Conspiracy is a group of bikers, truckers, and bounty hunters that hunt for demons, for profit, as paid by angels. The angels pay in weird stuff, like for example, healing terminal illnesses. The angels give them angelic script tattoos that give them nifty abilities, like the ability to punch demons and force them to take their true forms. <br /> <br /> When I was initially talking to Rose (the writer for that chapter) about the Conspiracy, I think I described them as &quot;Roadhouse meets Frailty&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T02:08:33-08:00","id":22208,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to seeing how that one turns out, for spy stories bikers and truckers seems like a pretty unusual direction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=21851#post21851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm lovin' it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think Mac Attax gets the magic into every Happy Meal? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T02:58:46-08:00","id":22219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22195#post22195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Demon-centric Conspiracy is a group of bikers, truckers, and bounty hunters that hunt for demons, for profit, as paid by angels. The angels pay in weird stuff, like for example, healing terminal illnesses. The angels give them angelic script tattoos that give them nifty abilities, like the ability to punch demons and force them to take their true forms.<br /> <br /> When I was initially talking to Rose (the writer for that chapter) about the Conspiracy, I think I described them as &quot;Roadhouse meets Frailty&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>that sounds... cool, actually. I mean, Demon as all about spying and trying to hide from the God Machine, right? And suddenly you have a group which is the manifestation of blunt force- they even punch them so hard to are forced into true form! Just from imagining the Demon's reaction (which is &quot;what the fuck is going on?!&quot;) I can't stop but starting to laugh an evil laughter :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T03:01:47-08:00","id":22221,"title":"","content":"I didn't think about that angle LostLight, but I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T05:17:59-08:00","id":22278,"title":"","content":"I like this Conspiracy, it can be really plug-n-play. I do understand it could be difficult to play as a PC though... unless of course, there is an &quot;end justifies the means&quot; angle in there somewhere. Maybe you're family was part of the cult of one of the Arisen, worshipping it and waiting for its return.... at which moment it wiped out your whole family. Payback time.<br /> <br /> Also, what kind of options are there for starting with Dread Powers during character creation?<br /> <br /> I also wonder whether there'll be a sidebar on the Faithful and Slashers... seems like there could be an interesting overlap there.<br /> <br /> Also also, if I understand correctly, no Conspiracies and Compacts for Promethean, Changeling and Geist? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1355,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","user":"horvagab","date":". 12-03-2013, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T06:54:49-08:00","id":22312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22208#post22208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to seeing how that one turns out, for spy stories bikers and truckers seems like a pretty unusual direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;bounty hunter&quot; motif fits the &quot;Cover vs. Compromise&quot; dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:11:33-08:00","id":22315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22278#post22278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also also, if I understand correctly, no Conspiracies and Compacts for Promethean, Changeling and Geist? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>that would make me into a sad person.. I mean, I hoped for at least a compact for each splat. After all, conspiracies usually needs more wordcount because of the endowments (unless their endowments are something similar to the ones of the Faithful, the Promethean Brotherhood or C&amp;C's Network 0)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:59:23-08:00","id":22338,"title":"","content":"A few opinions ON the Faithful that seem appropriate...<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: <i>...go on.</i><br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group: Primitive practices have led to major breakthroughs in the history of pharmaceuticals. Without knowledge of the biological mechanics involved, many isolated societies and social-groups have long known through experimentation which rare plants or animal parts to consume to treat certain ailments. Field researchers are advised not to ignore potential new resources employed by backward primitives and cults who may have made utilitarian discoveries through trial and error.<br /> <br /> VASCU: The Newcastle Cannibal Case remains open.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T08:19:35-08:00","id":22349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22278#post22278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also also, if I understand correctly, no Conspiracies and Compacts for Promethean, Changeling and Geist? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately not. I can see what I can do, but we're super late in the process to make any significant changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T08:30:01-08:00","id":22356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22349#post22349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not. I can see what I can do, but we're super late in the process to make any significant changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love more material, but I wouldn't want anything cut out of a need for parallel coverage. I mean, in a perfect world, each chapter of this book would be a full length book in their own right, but if that's not possible, that's what fan material is for.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, if anything does need to be cut, I'd encourage treating &quot;how to do this splat in HtV&quot; material as most expendable. Most people who want to do fae in HtV will be fae fans who are likely to have CtL. Coverage of the Hunters themselves is thus more valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:03:22-08:00","id":22403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22349#post22349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not. I can see what I can do, but we're super late in the process to make any significant changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, and I think it's a bad idea to force creativity... though if this book does well is there a chance to see conspiracies for those factions as a seperate PDF product down the line? Or some of the supplemental Conspiracies (Vascu, Cainite, etc...) getting a Compact &amp; Conspiracies treatment? I'd love t o see how VASCU deals with a few of the factions, Changeling and Geist foremost<br /> <br /> Also, how does this Endowment interact with Werewolf Dominions (I think?) and Witch Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1355,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","user":"horvagab","date":". 12-03-2013, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:56:34-08:00","id":22442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=22312#post22312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the &quot;bounty hunter&quot; motif fits the &quot;Cover vs. Compromise&quot; dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, but making the bounty hunters bikers and truckers was an unusual directions. Making them &quot;professional espionage people&quot;, like the Unchained themselves, would have been the &quot;usual direction&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"