in.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:02:52-08:00","id":25755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Glamourweaver:<br /> I mean, in a perfect world, each chapter of this book would be a full length book in their own right, but if that's not possible, that's what fan material is for.</b> </div> </div> </div>Considering you already came up with the perfect conspiracies for Promethean and Geist (the Ma'asi Merkavah and KSI21 respectively), maybe we can blame you for there not being new ones in the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:57:12-08:00","id":25776,"title":"","content":"KSI21 is a brilliant concept and I can't wait to see it; but I don't see what makes it a foil to Sin-Eaters or Ghosts. I'm not sure what book it really belongs in, maybe just a standalone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T01:19:00-08:00","id":27055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=25776#post25776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">KSI21 is a brilliant concept and I can't wait to see it; but I don't see what makes it a foil to Sin-Eaters or Ghosts. I'm not sure what book it really belongs in, maybe just a standalone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well those are the supernaturals they deal with most, since they're in twilight, and that's their original specific research mandate. But it's true they aren't monofocused the way the Order of the Knights of Saint George, Les Mysteres, or the Cainite Heresy are.<br /> <br /> I'd roughly put it on par with Malleus' vampire focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-10-2013, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T07:16:26-08:00","id":29890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>LostLight:</b><br /> So whose up for reviving Grave Robbers and Torch Bearers? </div> </div> </div>Reviving them as such is somewhat pointless. Had they worked out, they'd have included attempts to render the critters in Hunter terms and cover the existing groups' responses to them, the way Dream Catchers did. But Mortal Remains is going to do all that. Which isn't to say that a crowdsourced set of organisations to give each critter a full set of four couldn't be fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Glamourweaver:</b><br /> Well those are the supernaturals they deal with most, since they're in twilight, and that's their original specific research mandate. But it's true they aren't monofocused the way the Order of the Knights of Saint George, Les Mysteres, or the Cainite Heresy are.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that they still count as a foil to the Sin-Eaters, just not in the usually expected fashion. Firstly, they're the closest you're going to get to a technological analogue to the Bound, even if you could also describe them as a technological analogue to the shaman. Second, this paragraph from Geist, page 31:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;According to legend, the Sharaska began with hypothermia and drowning experiments during Stalin's regime. By 1950, researchers supposedly discovered a way to produce Sin-Eaters with controlled NDEs at a 1% success rate - and a mortality rate of at least 75%. ... There are numerous rumours that the conspiracy still exists, with agents spread across the world - even that they manipulate other governments into reproducing the original experiments to increase their numbers.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Barring a bizarre coincidence, KSI shares its origin with a pattern of experiments that produced Sin-Eaters - or else it became the subject of legend among them. Either way, while it might not be a foil in the cultural sense, it certainly is in a historical one. (Although while I describe KSI as perfect for Geist, I'd also extend the same accolade to the Brotherhood Prizrakov (plus they have rich interaction potential).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 12-14-2013, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T08:13:24-08:00","id":29917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=29890#post29890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reviving them as such is somewhat pointless. Had they worked out, they'd have included attempts to render the critters in Hunter terms and cover the existing groups' responses to them, the way Dream Catchers did. But Mortal Remains is going to do all that. Which isn't to say that a crowdsourced set of organisations to give each critter a full set of four couldn't be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well Mortal Remains is going to do that, but there's still the other three chapters and chances are there'll be room to expand on what Mortal Remains says.<br /> <br /> I mean my plan for Dream Catchers is to go through and try and focus things so that they can be read as an addition to Mortal Remains as well as independently; Torch Bearers and Grave Robbers could do the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=29890#post29890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that they still count as a foil to the Sin-Eaters, just not in the usually expected fashion. Firstly, they're the closest you're going to get to a technological analogue to the Bound, even if you could also describe them as a technological analogue to the shaman. Second, this paragraph from Geist, page 31</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not so much that they're a technological analogue, but how does KSI-21 or the Brotherhood Prizrakov relate to the theme of second chances? That's what's getting me.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I have an idea now. The Eastern Orthodox Church's hunters.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters died and came back for a second chance. The EOC Just. Wont. Die.<br /> Sin-Eaters live wild and free. The EOC hunters stay because of a deep belief in duty.<br /> Sin-Eaters are dynamic. The EOC is an old and traditional religion.<br /> <br /> I see the EOC has having been a thriving Hunter Conspiracy in the vein of the MM until they were hit badly by the Nazi's, indirectly it was just a really bad time for Eastern Europe, and then the Communists tried to suppress them intentionally and did a pretty good job of it. So for decades the dead killed by WWII, Nazi atrocoties and Soviet atrocities are starting to rise from their graves while the group best placed to do something about it (KSI-29 dosn't exist yet and the Brotherhood Prizrakov don't care that much) is getting weaker and weaker.<br /> <br /> But the EOC Just. Wont. Die, and by their fingernails they're clawing themselves back from oblivion to put the dead back in their graves.<br /> <br /> <br /> KSI-21 and the Brotherhood Prizrakov are cool and they have great potentual for Sin-Eater interaction, but neither of them tie into Second Chances; the Grave Robbers Conspiracy really should do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:25:27-08:00","id":30042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=29917#post29917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well Mortal Remains is going to do that, but there's still the other three chapters and chances are there'll be room to expand on what Mortal Remains says.<br /> <br /> I mean my plan for Dream Catchers is to go through and try and focus things so that they can be read as an addition to Mortal Remains as well as independently; Torch Bearers and Grave Robbers could do the same.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that they're a technological analogue, but how does KSI-21 or the Brotherhood Prizrakov relate to the theme of second chances? That's what's getting me.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I have an idea now. The Eastern Orthodox Church's hunters.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters died and came back for a second chance. The EOC Just. Wont. Die.<br /> Sin-Eaters live wild and free. The EOC hunters stay because of a deep belief in duty.<br /> Sin-Eaters are dynamic. The EOC is an old and traditional religion.<br /> <br /> I see the EOC has having been a thriving Hunter Conspiracy in the vein of the MM until they were hit badly by the Nazi's, indirectly it was just a really bad time for Eastern Europe, and then the Communists tried to suppress them intentionally and did a pretty good job of it. So for decades the dead killed by WWII, Nazi atrocoties and Soviet atrocities are starting to rise from their graves while the group best placed to do something about it (KSI-29 dosn't exist yet and the Brotherhood Prizrakov don't care that much) is getting weaker and weaker.<br /> <br /> But the EOC Just. Wont. Die, and by their fingernails they're clawing themselves back from oblivion to put the dead back in their graves.<br /> <br /> <br /> KSI-21 and the Brotherhood Prizrakov are cool and they have great potentual for Sin-Eater interaction, but neither of them tie into Second Chances; the Grave Robbers Conspiracy really should do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also contrast the theme with the hunter conspiracy, rather than embrace it. KSI-21, however, could be all about modern Russia's &quot;second chance&quot; at a great power through the mechanism of occult science. Can't keep up scientifically, economically or militarily with the United States or China, but Putin can decide to outright break longstanding agreements between nations not to attempt to harness occult power. Make it a Hunter Conspiracy that, by its connection to modern Russia's resurgent imperial ambition, is breaking the rule of secrecy.<br /> <br /> Also, where can I find KSI-21 and the Brotherhood Prizakov? I have only been able to figure out what you guys are talking about second-hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:42:37-08:00","id":30053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3436-conspiracy-the-brotherhood-prizrakov\">The Brotherhood Prizakov are here</a><br /> <br /> KSI-29 exists only in Glamourweaver's head at the moment (sadly), but it's basically Orpheus if it was run by the KGB.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for your idea. The Brotherhood Prizakov might work better than KSI-29 for that; given that they're one of the worlds economic powerhouses and I suppose the contrast beteween evil capatlistic overlords and the predominantly poor and alternative Sin-Eaters who escaped the grinding gears of wage slavery also has merit. Though I do also like the contrast between the undead and the people who Will. Not. Die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T18:28:04-08:00","id":30671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=29890#post29890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that they still count as a foil to the Sin-Eaters, just not in the usually expected fashion. Firstly, they're the closest you're going to get to a technological analogue to the Bound, even if you could also describe them as a technological analogue to the shaman. Second, this paragraph from Geist, page 31:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;According to legend, the Sharaska began with hypothermia and drowning experiments during Stalin's regime. By 1950, researchers supposedly discovered a way to produce Sin-Eaters with controlled NDEs at a 1% success rate - and a mortality rate of at least 75%. ... There are numerous rumours that the conspiracy still exists, with agents spread across the world - even that they manipulate other governments into reproducing the original experiments to increase their numbers.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Barring a bizarre coincidence, KSI shares its origin with a pattern of experiments that produced Sin-Eaters - or else it became the subject of legend among them. Either way, while it might not be a foil in the cultural sense, it certainly is in a historical one. (Although while I describe KSI as perfect for Geist, I'd also extend the same accolade to the Brotherhood Prizrakov (plus they have rich interaction potential).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NICE CATCH! Working that in now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-16-2013, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T05:59:40-08:00","id":30924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>TheKingsRaven:</b><br /> It's not so much that they're a technological analogue, but how does KSI-21 or the Brotherhood Prizrakov relate to the theme of second chances? That's what's getting me. </div> </div> </div>About as much as the Cainite Heresy are about personal horror, Les Mysteres are about savage fury, or your own Office of the Lord Stewards are about beautiful madness - which is to say not much, and I don't think that's a particular problem. Those phrases are about games where those beings are the protagonists - corresponding Hunter material, where those beings default to antagonists and other problems, can draw on it but shouldn't be beholden to it.<br /> <br /> Really, though I prefer to express the parallels and perpendiculars of &quot;corresponded&quot; hunter groups in Watsonian rather than Doylist terms - ie, in terms of the things <i>they'd</i> care about. The Cainites have dropped out of the world, and share their blood for power and identity (meanwhile the three Night Stalkers compacts focus on protectorates that vampires are particluarly likely to attack). Les Mysteres serve the Hisil spirits and hate werewolves because their patrons do. The Lord Stewards hold together a dangerous world through the power of agreements (and while one of the DC compacts is about beautiful madness, it's as a concrete goal they strive for). Likewise, Sin-Eaters claim death and its treasures as their right, and also as their right to extend and revoke the privilege of access to it for others - the Brotherhood Prizrakov makes makes the same claim, and had a worldview in which geists and bound are the big bads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I have an idea now. The Eastern Orthodox Church's hunters.<br /> Sin-Eaters died and came back for a second chance. The EOC Just. Wont. Die.<br /> Sin-Eaters live wild and free. The EOC hunters stay because of a deep belief in duty.<br /> Sin-Eaters are dynamic. The EOC is an old and traditional religion. </div> </div> </div>Which isn't to say that this paragraph doesn't make for a nice bonus; I just don't think it's the best starting point.<br /> <br /> (As it happens, I decided just yesterday to dust off the Pazitors).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>glamourweaver:</b><br /> NICE CATCH! Working that in now. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T06:24:18-08:00","id":30933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=30924#post30924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About as much as the Cainite Heresy are about personal horror, Les Mysteres are about savage fury, or your own Office of the Lord Stewards are about beautiful madness - which is to say not much, and I don't think that's a particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well the Cainites are about personal Horror. Les Mysteries aren't about savage fury but they've very much &quot;about&quot; spirit-world-border police. They just aproach it from the opposite angle. Werewolves keep the two worlds apart, Les Mysteries try and help them harmoniously fit together (then there's the bit about being duped which <i>completely ruins</i> the theme and... I'll stop before I start ranting).<br /> <br /> In fact the Lord Stewards, on whom I can speak authoritatively, are the same. The Core of Changeling is all about &quot;where do I go next&quot;, about building a life for yourself. The Lord Stewards are about <i>building a life for other people</i>. Or at least building a framework in which other people can build their lives.<br /> <br /> In fact I interpret all four of the the Dream Catcher's organisations as a Doylist foil to Changeling. The Lord Stewards I just said. Searchlight ties into the themes of kidnapping. The Wilde Society fit Beautiful Madness. The Sons are a harmonious union of two worlds (modern and iron age) to contrast with the Changeling struggle to balance two worlds. (Though that's a minor theme in the Sons, brotherhood and warriorhood come first).<br /> <br /> I'm really pleased with how that works, and how all four groups are designed to appeal to different players or basically entirely different games that are possible within the themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, you prefer Watsonian. I prefer Doylist, though I do not think the two have to be in conflict.<br /> <br /> Finally though, I would say that I consider the core of Werewolf to be &quot;spirit world border patrol&quot; not &quot;savage fury&quot;. However I do consider the core of Geist to be &quot;second chances&quot;. Just something that will help make where I'm coming from clearer.<br /> <br /> Those phrases are about games where those beings are the protagonists - corresponding Hunter material, where those beings default to antagonists and other problems, can draw on it but shouldn't be beholden to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/21487-hunter-mortal-remains-preview-the-faithful-of-shulpae?p=30924#post30924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As it happens, I decided just yesterday to dust off the Pazitors).</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually have a full write up of them (the old Compact though, not the new Conspiracy I'm thinking off now). I'm not sure why I never posted them, I'll do so later today when I get a chance.<br /> <br /> Then you can critise me for doing it wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> like how I renamed them The Order of St Anthony. But of course you're free to steal anything you like for your write up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T15:00:06-08:00","id":31237,"title":"","content":"bad russian accent/ &quot;KSI does not give second chances&quot; / bad russian accent<br /> <br /> More seriously though, the most overt way they play foil for Sin-Eaters is that while the Bound serve the interests of death in the living world, they serve the interests of a mortal state into the realms of the dead. They keep the ghosts of the past at bay so that a nation built on top of so many countless dead can move forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T15:08:44-08:00","id":31244,"title":"","content":"How close are they to being done btw? I really want to read these guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/fo